-- title:
--   Completed blow-up chart C[J/a] at P in the Drinfeld model
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. The coefficient field $L$ has characteristic zero, $\zeta \in L$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta) = e^{2\pi i/q}$. The level group is $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$, required by `hH₁` to be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{Laurent}(L)$, required by `hK` to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the subfield generated over $L$ by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars, of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$.
--
--   The base $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with algebraically closed residue field, with $L$ as fraction field, with $q$ in its maximal ideal (`hAq`), with $\zeta$ in the image of $A \to L$ (`hζA`), and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$. The element $j \in K$ is required by `hj` to have Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion of the classical $j$-function, and is nonzero. The element $\varpi$ generates the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hϖ`), and `hϖt` requires $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   The relevant chart algebra is `chartAlgFin A K j`, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$; write $C$ for it. The ideal $y \subseteq C$ is maximal, contains the image of $\varpi$, and is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of elements $j_0$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a single universally quantified existence statement, summarised here) requires, for every point $z$ of the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) at which the germ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of `XFin A K j = Spec C` mapping to $z$ and supersingular in the above sense, the existence of: a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ carrying $\varpi$ to a generator of the maximal ideal, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v - fu)$, subject to seven compatibility clauses: $e$ sends germs of constants from $A$ to their images $C(\sigma a)$; the chart algebra $C$ is stable under every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ attached via `IsLevelAutAt` to $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; such a $\tau$ acts trivially modulo $y'$ when $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$; each such $\tau$ induces an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing constants, linear to second order with matrix $M$ congruent to $c\gamma$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W$, with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, with $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, and with $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; primes of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$ with tangent directions independent modulo $q$ have distinct contractions to the stalk; membership in the contraction of such a prime is characterised by integrality of all Laurent coefficients; and [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $C$ and its difference from a suitable $a_0 \in A$ has image $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0 \ge 1$ whose leading form satisfies an explicit unit condition.
--
--   A point $z$ of `TwoChartIntegralModel A K j` is then fixed, together with the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$, the assumption $\varpi_z \in \mathfrak{m}$ (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'`, and `hy'y`, which identifies $y'$ with $y$. Concrete witness data at $z$ is given: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, power series $f_1$, units $u_1, v_1$ with $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of the stalk at $z$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` requires of this data exactly the seven clauses listed above.
--
--   The ideal $J \subseteq C$ is required by `hJ` to be the infimum of the ideals obtained as follows: for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ which preserves $C$, take the contraction along $\tau|_C$ of the contraction along $\Psi = e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ of $\mathfrak{M} = (\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t), \mathrm{mk}_S X_0, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1)$. Here $\mathrm{germY} : C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ is the composite of the inverses of the $\Gamma$–$\operatorname{Spec}$ isomorphism and of the comparison isomorphism for `ιFin A K j` on $\top$, followed by the germ map at $z$ on the open image of `ιFin A K j`, and $\mathrm{toC}$ is the map from the stalk to its adic completion.
--
--   Further auxiliary data is assumed: the $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x : \exists\, i \in J,\ x\varpi_t = i\}$ (`hB`); a valuation subring $W \subseteq K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`); `hR1`, that $C \le B$ and every element of $K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and $B/(\varpi)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that $y$ is the contraction of $\mathfrak{m}_W$ to $C$, and that $W$ is the set of fractions $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h$ a unit at $W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses), that for any $(\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2)$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$, compatible with reduction from $A$ and equivariant for level automorphisms through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) at an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under level automorphisms; that every prime of $B$ over $\varpi$ arises as the image of $\mathfrak{m}_W$ under a level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that $\varpi$ divides any element of $B$ lying in all translates of $\mathfrak{m}_W$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ preserves $W$. Finally, `hjK` and `hjC` place [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) in $K$ and in $C$, and $m \ge 1$ satisfies $\varpi^m = \varpi_t w$ for a unit $w$ (`hmt`).
--
--   The blow-up data is: $a \in C$ with $a \in J$ and $a \ne 0$ in $K$; the $A$-subalgebra $B_a \subseteq K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x : \exists\, i \in J,\ xa = i\}$ (`hBa`); and a maximal ideal $P \subseteq B_a$ whose contraction to $C$ is $y$ (`hPy`).
--
--   With $\Psi = e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY} : C \to S$, with $L_a =$ `Localization.Away (Ψ a)`, with $\mathfrak{M} = (\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi_t), \mathrm{mk}_S X_0, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1)$, and with $R \subseteq L_a$ the subring generated by the image of $S$ together with $\{x : \exists\, i \in \mathfrak{M},\ x \cdot \Psi a = i \text{ in } L_a\}$, the conclusion asserts: $\Psi a$ is a non-zero-divisor of $S$; $\Psi a \in \mathfrak{M}$; and there exist a ring homomorphism $\Phi : B_a \to L_a$ taking all its values in $R$ such that $\Phi$ agrees with $\Psi$ on the elements of $C$ that lie in $B_a$, and such that for $x \in B_a$ and $i \in J$ with $xa = i$ in $K$ one has $\Phi(x)\cdot \Psi a = \Psi i$ in $L_a$; and there exist a maximal ideal $P' \subseteq R$ such that the contraction of $P'$ along $\Phi$ is exactly $P$ (for $b \in B_a$, $\Phi b \in P'$ iff $b \in P$) and such that every $s \in S$ lying in the ideal $(\mathrm{mk}_S C(\sigma_1\varpi), \mathrm{mk}_S X_0, \mathrm{mk}_S X_1)$ whose image in $L_a$ lies in $R$ has that image in $P'$; and finally a ring isomorphism $T$ from the $P$-adic completion of $B_a$ onto the $P'$-adic completion of $R$ compatible with $\Phi$, in the sense that $T$ carries the canonical image of $b \in B_a$ to the canonical image of $\Phi b \in R$.
--
--   This identifies the completed local ring of the blow-up chart $C[J/a]$ of the integral model at a supersingular point, at a maximal ideal lying over $y$, with the completed local ring of the corresponding blow-up $S[\mathfrak{M}/\Psi a]$ of the Drinfeld power-series chart, together with the comparison map $\Phi$ on the level of the chart algebras themselves. It is the transfer step which makes the explicit two-variable model available after blowing up, and it is used in the subsequent description of the completed blow-up chart by a $uv$-crossing model with prescribed tangent and centre data.
